[1mWhat the program does:[22m [38;5;10mdriver a b c[0m parses three arguments with [38;5;10matof[0m, runs Quake III's [38;5;10mVectorNormalizeFast[0m (fast inverse square root, one Newton iteration), and prints [38;5;10m"%f %f %f\n"[0m. Wrong argument count prints [38;5;10margv[0] requires 4 inputs[0m to stderr and exits 1.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mBugs found and fixed[22m (all recorded in [38;5;10mtranslation/ERRORS.md[0m):[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [1m[38;5;10mas f32[0m dropped the NaN sign bit.[22m [38;5;10mdriver -nan 1 nan[0m printed [38;5;10m-nan nan nan[0m instead of [38;5;10m-nan -nan nan[0m. Rust leaves float-to-float cast NaN payloads unspecified, and LLVM's constant folder turns [38;5;10mfff8000000000000[0m into [38;5;10m+7fc00000[0m. It only bites because LLVM can see through the inlined [38;5;10matof[0m and fold the [38;5;10mfptrunc[0m; at runtime [38;5;10mcvtsd2ss[0m preserves the sign. Fixed with explicit sign-preserving [38;5;10mnarrow_to_f32[0m/[38;5;10mwiden_to_f64[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
2. [1mLLVM reorders commutative float operands, which changes [3mwhich[23m NaN x86 returns.[22m [38;5;10mmulss[0m/[38;5;10maddss[0m return the destination operand's NaN if it has one, else the source's — so operand order decides the output sign. [38;5;10mv[0]*=k; v[1]*=k; v[2]*=k[0m vectorized into one [38;5;10mmulps[0m with [38;5;10mk[0m as destination, making all three lanes return [38;5;10mk[0m's NaN. Fixed with a new [38;5;10msrc/fpu.rs[0m whose [38;5;10mfmul[0m/[38;5;10mfadd[0m/[38;5;10mfsub[0m make the destination operand explicit, plus preserving C's exact grouping ([38;5;10mDotProduct[0m associates left; [38;5;10mx2*y*y[0m is [38;5;10m(x2*y)*y[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
3. [1mx86's invalid-operation result is a [3mnegative[23m NaN.[22m [38;5;10mdriver inf 0 0[0m prints [38;5;10m-inf -nan -nan[0m, because [38;5;10m0 * -inf[0m yields the QNaN indefinite [38;5;10m0xFFC00000[0m. LLVM folds it to positive. Now returned explicitly.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
